{"skill":{"slug":"local-places","displayName":"Local Places"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545354524,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"pyproject.toml","size":481,"sha256":"5aecf8fa98db53c55d40583f97a6e435157e75c082dae3a3152fae021d6c6154","contentType":"application/toml"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2483,"sha256":"20e1cc6473c9704775076f8aa48b01ba6b0ac8006e8841f64927c962fe17561f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SERVER_README.md","size":2047,"sha256":"21fccf3087b58eb58e6da5368533164b4f40f1cef12bd20c228c769f1d44e681","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"src/local_places/__init__.py","size":48,"sha256":"b576d15ec3b4344fd45759081e26534d0407d1f8f45362a8c7136eb2efe0ceb3","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/local_places/google_places.py","size":9111,"sha256":"358207890bf1244ed74ad26dc7ecde2e17281ab26944e30e5bb5d3a0cdb50ebe","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/local_places/schemas.py","size":3030,"sha256":"2eec353cb92e27b317c1255534f8535a6f46ced85e857d6887bd89cc1c81a109","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/local_places/main.py","size":1776,"sha256":"6959470c3fdb6d7342b7b9e6eadf2d08c046ff0450b449b29c54345ca7977d52","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2278,"sha256":"e0442a6d792d5e36d39731312e7e1412622d0c6322fb9593ae6ac1e9874597df","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013667145,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"9e50379d7c3204ad12c2682e0ce1af0c387a5082b58c4eb92014e628c35e446a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/9e50379d7c3204ad12c2682e0ce1af0c387a5082b58c4eb92014e628c35e446a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: local-places\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle sets up a local FastAPI server to proxy requests to the Google Places API, requiring a `GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY` for authentication with Google. All network communication is directed to the official Google API endpoint or the local server. The `SKILL.md` provides clear, functional instructions for the AI agent to interact with the local API for its stated purpose, without any evidence of prompt injection attempts to subvert the agent's behavior. There are no indicators of data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation across any of the files.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159614710},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":83,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789013667145},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill does what it claims, but its included server can expose an unauthenticated Google Places API-key proxy beyond localhost, creating billing, quota, and location-privacy risk.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The environment requirements are proportionate for a Places proxy, but GOOGLE_PLACES_BASE_URL can redirect requests while the code still attaches GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY, and validation errors log complete request bodies that may contain sensitive location text or coordinates.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation uses uv, editable Python package installation, and standard PyPI dependencies. No remote payload execution, persistence hooks, or obfuscated install behavior were found, but dependencies are broad lower bounds rather than pinned versions.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The main SKILL.md setup binds uvicorn to 127.0.0.1, but SERVER_README.md and the Python __main__ entry bind to 0.0.0.0 without authentication, authorization, or rate limiting. That conflicts with the localhost framing and can expose API-key-backed endpoints to other network clients.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No system persistence, scheduled tasks, memory poisoning, or privilege escalation mechanisms were found. The main persistence concern is operational logging of full invalid request bodies, not a durable backdoor.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The core purpose is coherent: a FastAPI service and agent instructions for resolving locations, searching places, and fetching place details through Google Places. Use of a Google Places API key and network calls is purpose-aligned and disclosed in the skill metadata and setup instructions.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review before installing or running. Use only loopback binding, avoid the SERVER_README.md 0.0.0.0 command unless you add authentication and network controls, restrict the Google API key in Google Cloud, do not set GOOGLE_PLACES_BASE_URL to untrusted hosts, and avoid submitting sensitive home, work, or routine locations unless you accept that they may be sent to Google and written to logs on validation errors.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The API key and local HTTP service are expected for this skill and are partly disclosed in SKILL.md metadata, so this finding is downgraded as a transparency note rather than an independent reason for Review.\n[TP4] expected: Location resolution and place details are part of the documented Quick Start and conversation flow, so this is not tool poisoning. The real issue is that the localhost framing is weakened by other server entry points using 0.0.0.0.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending place queries and location strings to Google is inherent in a Google Places API proxy and is indicated by the description, but the artifact lacks a clear privacy notice about sensitive location data and logging.\n[SC4] expected: Uvicorn is expected for FastAPI serving. The dependency concern is limited because the declared lower bound is modern, but the unpinned range and network-exposed development server increase operational risk.\n[T05] unexpected: This finding is supported by artifact evidence: SERVER_README.md recommends --host 0.0.0.0 --reload, main.py also defaults __main__ to 0.0.0.0, and the endpoints proxy Google Places requests using the operator's API key without authentication.\n[T09] unexpected: The arbitrary GOOGLE_PLACES_BASE_URL override is not necessary for normal use and can send the Google API key to a non-Google destination if the environment is misconfigured or influenced.\n[T09] unexpected: Logging complete validation request bodies is not needed for the skill purpose and can retain sensitive free-text locations, coordinates, or accidental secrets in logs.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013667145}}}}}